Context
  Asked to have 0.3.0 fix the nomenclature and point the publish metadata at
  https://wal.sh/tools/plugins/guile-skills/ and its children.

Deviations
  Only the parent page and /docs/ are referenced. The per-skill children were probed
  and all 404, so linking them would have shipped dead URLs.

  The skill nomenclature itself needed nothing: the guile- prefix came out in 0.2.0
  and a grep of the shipped prose found no residue. The workspace directories keep
  their old names deliberately -- recorded evidence.

Considerations
  The channels correction came from a worktree experiment and reverses what
  surfaces.org claimed. I had described a channel as presupposing an MCP server and a
  credential, which is half right: the MCP server is real, the credential belongs to
  the ingress rather than the mechanism, and there is no listener at all.

  Directory state at the time of this commit: v0.2.0 is still SCANNING and v0.1.4 is
  live. Publishing 0.3.0 queues a second scan; whether that serialises is not known.

Timeline
  2026-09-29, nexus, claude 2.1.261, as dsp-dr. gmake checks green; validate --strict
